      "source": [
        {
          "question": "q-32128",
          "field": "selection",
          "attribute": "answer-field/correct",
          "value": [
            ":answer.type/math",
            "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A"
          ],
          "category": "reviewed_ma_solution",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/answer-source-reviews.json",
          "file_sha256": "87952292242d55822add9809f3184007cdbccb6c67ff7974d75e8a2332c659e1",
          "reviewer_session": "01a118cc-89a0-7c90-9221-d6599ae13bca",
          "rationale": "Applying R2:=R2-3R3 to the identity gives E=[[1,0,0],[0,1,-3],[0,0,1]]. Left multiplication EA replaces row 2 of A with row 2 minus three times row 3, preserving the other rows. Therefore original option 2 and the stored answer are correct. Right multiplication AE generally performs a different column operation. This is a source-backed derived judgment from the original operation and authentic worked solution. The Incorrect grade concerns submitted option 3, not this reviewed answer.",
