      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-4733",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "We need to find a matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_2 := R_2-2R_1$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/assets/8d015aca8950073c165d53b14f86f0e65a207438ad901ce82f85f65bb8347519.png)",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060012/example-4733.json",
          "file_sha256": "e3fe4f43606eb0a95a9e71968d078cdc00d8e0c5e02ba3bedd54f6e86d5934d1"
        }
      ],
